{# Nothing booked yet. Built to the same shape as the saved page's empty
   state: name the state, say what will fill it, and offer the one action that
   does. What this replaced was a single "not found" image, which told a
   visitor that something was missing without saying what, why, or what to do
   about it -- and read as an error on a page that is working correctly. #}
<div class="text-center py-5">
    <i class="fas fa-plane-departure empty-state__icon"></i>
    <h2 class="h4 mt-3">No bookings yet</h2>
    <p class="text-muted mb-4">
        Once you book a flight it will be listed here, with its reference and the full itinerary.
    </p>
    <a href="/" class="btn btn-primary">Search for flights</a>
</div>
